# No Co-Author Commits

This project does not allow Cursor, Copilot, or any other AI/tool to be listed as a commit author or coauthor.

- Never add `Co-authored-by:` (or any coauthor/trailer attribution) to commit messages.
- Never pass `--trailer`, multi-author flags, or similar to attribute Cursor (`cursoragent@cursor.com`), Copilot, or any other AI/tool.
- Commit messages must attribute only the human author already configured in git.
- If a commit is created with a `Co-authored-by: Cursor` (or similar) trailer, remove it before push. Cursor may inject the trailer after `git commit`; do not leave it on the branch.
- Do not invent additional authors.
